         3,
         "During severe Negative Energy Balance (early lactation in cows; last 2–4 weeks of gestation in ewes carrying twins/triplets), intense hepatic gluconeogenesis drains mitochondrial **Oxaloacetate (OAA)**. Simultaneously, low insulin / high growth hormone and catecholamines mobilize massive adipose **NEFA** to the liver. Without sufficient OAA to condense with Acetyl-CoA (via citrate synthase) in the TCA cycle, Acetyl-CoA is shunted into **Ketogenesis** (**Acetoacetate, $\\beta$-Hydroxybutyrate [BHBA], and Acetone**), while surplus NEFA re-esterifies into triglycerides that cannot be exported fast enough as VLDL, causing **Hepatic Lipidosis (Fatty Liver)**.",
